# Rank 1583 / CVE-2023-3432: PlantUML's URL allowlist matched by
# string prefix, so a URL carrying userinfo -- https://plantuml.com@
# attacker.example/ -- passed the check because the prefix matched
# before the @ while the request went to the host after it (URL
# allowlist bypass, CWE-918/CWE-706; credit Agasthya Kasturi in the
# fix). forbiddenURL and isInUrlAllowList in
# src/net/sourceforge/plantuml/security/SURL.java checked
# startsWith(cleanPath(allow)) against the full URL string -- with a
# PATTERN_USERINFO regex that did not anchor its tail -- letting the
# userinfo segment impersonate the allowed host. Pool commit
# b32500bb61 is the real fix (COMMIT_OK -- "fix: improve filelist
# support and nwdiag", carrying the SURL hardening): both methods
# reject outright `if (full.contains("@"))`, and PATTERN_USERINFO
# anchors with $. No pool correction.
#
# ATTENTION, prefix-matched URL allowlists. The allowlist exists and
# runs -- its defeat is that string prefixes are not URL structure:
# userinfo, and any grammar element before the host, matches first,
# the same normalization-strength family as rank 1522 (bracket-blind
# hosts) and 1582 (the wildcard pattern). Nothing can ask "does the
# allowlist compare parsed hosts rather than string prefixes" --
# that is URL-structure vocabulary. A binding on PlantUML's own
# SURL would detect this tool rather than the weakness. Measured on
# the real code: scanning SURL.java reports zero findings at both
# revisions. No ENGINE-GAPS.md entry. No definition change shipped.
# Spec cve_rank1583 records the prefix-matched allowlist and the
# @-rejecting form, both asserting reject VYQL-RF-001: when
# url-structure vocabulary lands, the prefix form must flip to
# expect.

test "rank1583: the allowlist matches url prefixes"
  lang java
  file src/net/sourceforge/plantuml/security/SURL.java
  reject VYQL-RF-001
  code
  ```
  import java.util.List;

  public class SURL {
      private final List<String> urlAllowList;

      private boolean forbiddenURL(String full) {
          if (full.startsWith("https://") == false && full.startsWith("http://") == false)
              return true;
          return false;
      }

      private boolean isInUrlAllowList() {
          final String full = internal.toString();
          for (String allow : urlAllowList)
              if (full.startsWith(allow))
                  return true;
          return false;
      }

      public boolean isUrlAllowed(String internal) {
          return forbiddenURL(internal) == false && isInUrlAllowList();
      }
  }
  ```

test "rank1583: the fix rejects userinfo outright"
  lang java
  file src/net/sourceforge/plantuml/security/SURL.java
  reject VYQL-RF-001
  code
  ```
  import java.util.List;

  public class SURL {
      private final List<String> urlAllowList;

      private boolean forbiddenURL(String full) {
          // Thanks to Agasthya Kasturi
          if (full.contains("@"))
              return true;
          if (full.startsWith("https://") == false && full.startsWith("http://") == false)
              return true;
          return false;
      }

      private boolean isInUrlAllowList() {
          final String full = internal.toString();
          // Thanks to Agasthya Kasturi
          if (full.contains("@"))
              return false;
          for (String allow : urlAllowList)
              if (full.startsWith(allow))
                  return true;
          return false;
      }

      public boolean isUrlAllowed(String internal) {
          return forbiddenURL(internal) == false && isInUrlAllowList();
      }
  }
  ```
